  <div class="mainPageSection newsSection">
    <h2 class="title">News</h2>

    <div class="newsPost">
      <ul class="newsMeta">
        <li class="newsDate">April 4, 2026</li>
        <li class="newsAuthor"><img src="/images/phantoon.png" /> phantomsnake</li>
      </ul>
      <div class="newsBody">
        <p>
          We added a new NMG Low% category: <a href="/Leaderboard/IcePb">13% Ice-Pb</a>! Here's the announcement from the mod team:
        </p>
        <blockquote>
          <p>
            <b>Leaderboard Update - Low% reorganization</b>
          </p>
          <p>
            Hi Everyone - Following the recent community discussion and additional review from the SRC and DT leaderboard moderation teams, we're moving forward with an update to how 13% Underflow and related categories are handled across both leaderboards. The goal of this change is to give 13% the visibility and recognition it deserves, while preserving the integrity and historical relevance of 14% Ice.
          </p>
          <p>
            Decision Summary:<br/>
            Runs that utilize Underflow will now be considered a distinct ruleset.
            13% Underflow will be placed alongside NMG Low% on the Main Boards, and will be marked with an asterisk to indicate the modified ruleset.
          </p>
          <p>
            All L+R runs will be compiled on the Extension Boards.
          </p>
          <p>
            Main Boards will remain reserved for categories that can be completed on original hardware under normal SOCD rules.
          </p>
          <p>
            This approach reflects the strongest community and mod consensus: highlighting 13% without invalidating or overshadowing 14% Ice, while also keeping rulesets clearly defined and consistent across leaderboards.
          </p>
          <p>
            As always, feedback is welcome, and we appreciate everyone who contributed to the discussion, last month.
          </p>
        </blockquote>
      </div>
    </div>

    <a href="/News">Past News</a>
  </div>

